* TIMES.jl crafted case demo12_ls (reference/crafted.toml, 8 Nov 2026): demo12 variant 1,
* load shifting (docs/demo12-variants.md; eqactups.vda L127-158, EQ_SLSIFT; M1.3 change 24),
* added to TIMES_Demo demo12 (etsap-TIMES/TIMES_Demo @ 962db86, CC BY 4.0). Set up as
* TIMES-NZ's demand-flexibility processes are (a timeslice storage process at the DAYNITE
* level whose commodity is both its input and output, an activity group, STG_EFF and
* STG_SIFT): LSCOMELC shifts commercial electricity (COMELC) in both regions, up to 20% of
* it in REG1 (30% by 2050) and 10% in REG2; in REG2 the activity itself may also shift
* (STG_SIFT on ACT at the WD slice). No ACT_TIME, so the time-window terms are not used
* (demo12_lst adds them).
$ONEMPTY
$ONEPS
$ONWARNING
SET PRC
/
LSCOMELC 'Load shifting of commercial electricity'
/

SET COM_GRP
/
LSCOMELC_NRGO
/

SET COM_GMAP
/
REG1.LSCOMELC_NRGO.COMELC
REG2.LSCOMELC_NRGO.COMELC
/

SET PRC_MAP
/
REG1.STG.LSCOMELC
REG2.STG.LSCOMELC
/

SET PRC_TSL
/
REG1.LSCOMELC.DAYNITE
REG2.LSCOMELC.DAYNITE
/

SET PRC_ACTUNT
/
REG1.LSCOMELC.LSCOMELC_NRGO.PJ
REG2.LSCOMELC.LSCOMELC_NRGO.PJ
/

SET TOP
/
REG1.LSCOMELC.COMELC.IN
REG1.LSCOMELC.COMELC.OUT
REG2.LSCOMELC.COMELC.IN
REG2.LSCOMELC.COMELC.OUT
/

PARAMETER
STG_EFF ' '/
REG1.2005.LSCOMELC 0.95
REG2.2005.LSCOMELC 0.95
/

PARAMETER
STG_SIFT ' '/
REG1.2005.LSCOMELC.COMELC.ANNUAL 0.2
REG1.2050.LSCOMELC.COMELC.ANNUAL 0.3
REG2.2005.LSCOMELC.COMELC.ANNUAL 0.1
REG2.2005.LSCOMELC.ACT.WD 0.05
/
